# Modus Icons Usage Rules for Next.js

## 🎯 Core Principle: Use Valid Icon Names Only

**Always use valid Modus icon names.** Only the icons defined in the Modus icon library are guaranteed to render properly. Invalid icon names will not display correctly.

## 🚀 Icon Implementation Patterns

### ✅ Preferred: Direct HTML Usage with Tailwind Classes

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Basic icon usage
<i className="modus-icons">save_disk</i>

// ✅ CORRECT - Icon with text in button
<ModusWcButton color="primary">
  <i className="modus-icons mr-2">download</i>
  Download File
</ModusWcButton>

// ✅ CORRECT - Icon-only button
<ModusWcButton shape="circle" aria-label="Delete item">
  <i className="modus-icons">delete</i>
</ModusWcButton>
```

### ✅ Alternative: Using ModusButton Component

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Using ModusButton with icon prop
<ModusButton
  icon="save_disk"
  iconPosition="left"
  color="primary"
  onButtonClick={handleSave}
>
  Save File
</ModusButton>

// ✅ CORRECT - Icon-only button
<ModusButton
  icon="delete"
  iconPosition="only"
  color="danger"
  aria-label="Delete item"
/>
```

## 📏 Icon Sizing

### Using Tailwind Classes (Recommended)

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Using Tailwind text size classes
<i className="modus-icons text-xs">star</i>  {/* 11px */}
<i className="modus-icons text-sm">star</i>  {/* 14px */}
<i className="modus-icons text-base">star</i> {/* 16px (default) */}
<i className="modus-icons text-lg">star</i>   {/* 20px */}
<i className="modus-icons text-xl">star</i>   {/* 24px */}
<i className="modus-icons text-2xl">star</i>  {/* 30px */}
```

### Using Inline Styles

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Custom size with inline styles
<i className="modus-icons" style={{ fontSize: "24px" }}>star</i>

// ✅ CORRECT - Using ModusButton with custom sizing
<ModusButton
  icon="star"
  iconPosition="only"
  className="text-2xl"
/>
```

## 🎨 Icon Colors

### Using Modus Color Variables

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Using inline styles with Modus color variables
<i className="modus-icons" style={{ color: "var(--modus-wc-color-success)" }}>check</i>
<i className="modus-icons" style={{ color: "var(--modus-wc-color-warning)" }}>warning</i>
<i className="modus-icons" style={{ color: "var(--modus-wc-color-error)" }}>error</i>

// ✅ CORRECT - Using Tailwind classes with design system colors
<i className="modus-icons text-success">check</i>
<i className="modus-icons text-warning">warning</i>
<i className="modus-icons text-destructive">error</i>
```

### Using Design System Colors

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Using design system colors
<i className="modus-icons text-foreground">home</i>
<i className="modus-icons text-muted-foreground">info</i>
<i className="modus-icons text-primary">star</i>
```

## ♿ Accessibility Guidelines

### Decorative Icons (Default)

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Decorative icons (hidden from screen readers)
<i className="modus-icons">star</i>
<i className="modus-icons" aria-hidden="true">star</i>

// ✅ CORRECT - Using ModusButton for decorative icons
<ModusButton icon="star" iconPosition="only" />
```

### Functional Icons

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Icons that convey meaning
<ModusWcButton shape="circle" aria-label="Delete item">
  <i className="modus-icons">delete</i>
</ModusWcButton>

// ✅ CORRECT - Using ModusButton with proper accessibility
<ModusButton
  icon="delete"
  iconPosition="only"
  aria-label="Delete item"
  color="danger"
/>
```

