## 📋 Icon Implementation Checklist for Next.js

For every icon implementation:

- [ ] ✅ **Valid Icon Name**: Used only valid Modus icon names
- [ ] ✅ **Proper Implementation**: Used `<i className="modus-icons">` or `ModusButton` component
- [ ] ✅ **Tailwind Classes**: Used Tailwind classes for sizing (`text-xs`, `text-sm`, `text-lg`, etc.)
- [ ] ✅ **Modus Colors**: Used only Modus CSS color variables or design system colors
- [ ] ✅ **Accessibility**: Added `aria-label` for functional icons, kept decorative icons hidden
- [ ] ✅ **Proper Spacing**: Used Tailwind spacing classes (`mr-2`, `ml-2`) for icons with text
- [ ] ✅ **Semantic Usage**: Chose icons that match their intended meaning
- [ ] ✅ **Consistent Style**: Maintained consistent icon usage patterns across the app
- [ ] ✅ **CSS Import**: Ensured Modus icons CSS is imported in `globals.css`
- [ ] ✅ **Client Components**: Used `"use client"` directive when needed for interactive icons

## 🎯 Next.js Specific Requirements

### CSS Import Setup

```css
/* In globals.css - MUST be first */
@import url("https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@trimble-oss/modus-icons@1.17.0/dist/field-systems/fonts/modus-icons.css");
```

### Component Usage Patterns

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Direct HTML usage
<i className="modus-icons">icon_name</i>

// ✅ CORRECT - With Tailwind spacing
<i className="modus-icons mr-2">icon_name</i>

// ✅ CORRECT - Using ModusButton component
<ModusButton icon="icon_name" iconPosition="left">
  Button Text
</ModusButton>
```

---

**Remember: Icons should enhance usability and provide visual clarity. Always choose icons that clearly represent their function and maintain consistency throughout your Next.js application.**

